{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"178.165.59.111","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":81049,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f92de59bc02543087ae7fd03c5203471","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:&#039;Open sans&#039;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;Hello everybody.&lt;\/span&gt;\n&lt;span style=\"font-family:&#039;Open sans&#039;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;I noticed that some photographers are completely floppy&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/discuss.pixls.us\/images\/emoji\/emoji_one\/frowning.png?v=3\" title=\":frowning:\" alt=\"frowning.png?v=3\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:&#039;Open sans&#039;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;. Several times I encountered the case that the photographer made really good photos but did not edit them.&lt;\/span&gt;\n&lt;span style=\"font-family:&#039;Open sans&#039;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;What do you think: is it better to address third-party wedding-retouching companies..&lt;\/span&gt;\n&lt;span style=\"font-family:&#039;Open sans&#039;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;OR&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;\n&lt;span style=\"font-family:&#039;Open sans&#039;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;Is it better to contact the photographer for photo editing?&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1917767,"PostDate":1496061847,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">Hello everybody.<\/span><br><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">I noticed that some photographers are completely floppy\u00a0<\/span><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/discuss.pixls.us\/images\/emoji\/emoji_one\/frowning.png?v=3\" title=\":frowning:\" alt=\"frowning.png?v=3\"><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">\u00a0. Several times I encountered the case that the photographer made really good photos but did not edit them.<\/span><br><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">What do you think: is it better to address third-party wedding-retouching companies..<\/span><br><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">OR\u00a0<\/span><br><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">Is it better to contact the photographer for photo editing?<\/span><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"evgeniasafonova6@gmail.com","IpAddress":"178.165.59.111","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1496061611,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"https:\/\/bdw-stevewright.netdna-ssl.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"JoshN1","Id":288940,"Name":"JoshN1","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"189.205.241.131","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":81049,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"4e6385c65dddd5987a096dc55d5f421a","RawContent":"[quote name=\"JoshN1\" post=\"1917767\" timestamp=\"1496076247\"]\n[font=&#039;Open sans&#039;]Hello everybody.[\/font]\n[font=&#039;Open sans&#039;]I noticed that some photographers are completely floppy [\/font][img]https:\/\/discuss.pixls.us\/images\/emoji\/emoji_one\/frowning.png?v=3[\/img][font=&#039;Open sans&#039;] . Several times I encountered the case that the photographer made really good photos but did not edit them.[\/font]\n[font=&#039;Open sans&#039;]What do you think: is it better to address third-party wedding-retouching companies..[\/font]\n[font=&#039;Open sans&#039;]OR [\/font]\n[font=&#039;Open sans&#039;]Is it better to contact the photographer for photo editing?[\/font][\/quote]\nSpeaking as a wedding photographer myself, whether the photos are to be edited should be included in the wedding photography contract. Typically photographers will give you edited images, however, there are some photographers that offer \"shoot and burn\" services -- meaning they shoot the wedding, then put those files onto a disk or flash drive and deliver without post-processing or editing. Shoot and burn photographers are typically cheaper, but then you end up with photos that have not been edited.\n\nYou should definitely make sure you clarify this detail ahead of time before you hire your photographer and ensure that the details are included in your service contract.\n\nMy advice is to contact your photographer first before any third-party editor. There are also clauses in contracts that don&#039;t allow a photographer&#039;s photos to be edited by a third party source unless they give you permission. Hope that helps!","Attachments":[],"Id":1917780,"PostDate":1496335306,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>JoshN1, on 29 May 2017 - 12:44 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">Hello everybody.<\/span><br><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">I noticed that some photographers are completely floppy\u00a0<\/span><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/discuss.pixls.us\/images\/emoji\/emoji_one\/frowning.png?v=3\" title=\":frowning:\" alt=\"frowning.png?v=3\"><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">\u00a0. Several times I encountered the case that the photographer made really good photos but did not edit them.<\/span><br><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">What do you think: is it better to address third-party wedding-retouching companies..<\/span><br><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">OR\u00a0<\/span><br><span  style=\"font-family:'Open sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">Is it better to contact the photographer for photo editing?<\/span><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Speaking as a wedding photographer myself, whether the photos are to be edited should be included in the wedding photography contract. Typically photographers will give you edited images, however, there are some photographers that offer \"shoot and burn\" services -- meaning they shoot the wedding, then put those files onto a disk or flash drive and deliver without post-processing or editing. Shoot and burn photographers are typically cheaper, but then you end up with photos that have not been edited.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>You should definitely make sure you clarify this detail ahead of time before you hire your photographer and ensure that the details are included in your service contract.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My advice is to contact your photographer first before any third-party editor. There are also clauses in contracts that don't allow a photographer's photos to be edited by a third party source unless they give you permission. Hope that helps!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia;\"><strong>MARIESAM SANCHEZ PHOTOGRAPHY<\/strong><\/span><\/span><br>\nWEBSITE: <a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.mariesamsanchez.com\">www.mariesamsanchez.com<\/a><br>\nBLOG: <a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.mariesamsanchezblog.com\">www.mariesamsanchez.com<\/a><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.mariesamsanchez.com\/blog'>\/blog<\/a><br>\nCONTACT ME: <a  class=\"bbc_email\" href=\"mailto:mariesam.sanchez@gmail.com?subject=BDW%20Inquiry\" title=\"E-mail Link\">mariesam.sanchez@gmail.com<\/a><br><br><img src=\"http:\/\/i287.photobucket.com\/albums\/ll150\/msam007562\/063cb5c8-dbda-4822-87fe-ba3c0ebcdb7f.jpg\" alt=\"063cb5c8-dbda-4822-87fe-ba3c0ebcdb7f.jpg\">","Email":"mariesam.sanchez@gmail.com","IpAddress":"74.100.61.37","GroupId":38,"GroupName":"Moderators","JoinDate":1285939945,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"https:\/\/bdw-stevewright.netdna-ssl.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232833.jpg?_r=1422091823","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":220,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"MarieSamSanchezPhoto","Id":232833,"Name":"MarieSamSanchezPhoto","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"31.42.65.247","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":81049,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7de5b60ab33e36c2ad471945c851d214","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;\n&lt;span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0);\"&gt;We had a wedding two months ago. We faund great photos on the site&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;https:\/\/taraweddings.ca\/&#039;&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;text-align:center;\"&gt;Tara Weddings&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;and decided to order a photo session and video. It was really very cool, and high quality. You can watch their works. They are really cool.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1917950,"PostDate":1500889620,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>\n<span  style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">We had a wedding two months ago. We faund great photos on the site\u00a0<\/span><a href='https:\/\/taraweddings.ca\/' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'><span  style=\"font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;text-align:center\">Tara Weddings<\/span><\/a><span  style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt\">\u00a0<\/span><span  style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt\">\u00a0and decided to order a photo session and video. It was really very cool, and high quality. You can watch their works. They are really cool.<\/span><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"5linkstream5@gmail.com","IpAddress":"31.42.65.247","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1500887559,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"https:\/\/bdw-stevewright.netdna-ssl.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"KateMoll","Id":289166,"Name":"KateMoll","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":3,"TotalPages":1,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":0},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
